WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.425 --> 00:00:18.033
"Are you ready to sell some T-shirts?"

2
00:00:18.473 --> 00:00:22.495
Ally asked Mateo as they carried boxes onto the soccer field the next day.

3
00:00:22.975 --> 00:00:25.457
They had just picked up the T-shirts from the print shop.

4
00:00:26.818 --> 00:00:28.739
"I sure am," Mateo said.

5
00:00:29.539 --> 00:00:30.560
Ally looked at the field.

6
00:00:33.116 --> 00:00:35.517
"I hope lots of people show up to help out."

7
00:00:35.537 --> 00:00:38.518
"I don't think we have to worry about that."

8
00:00:39.259 --> 00:00:40.019
Mateo grinned.

9
00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:41.620
"Look at the field!"

10
00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:43.761
Kate and Bethany were there.

11
00:00:44.181 --> 00:00:47.222
And so was Barry, along with everyone from soccer camp.

12
00:00:50.364 --> 00:00:53.725
On the opposite side of the field, Ally saw even more people.

13
00:00:53.745 --> 00:00:59.047
"It looks like those people are already collecting signatures for our petition!"

14
00:00:59.788 --> 00:01:00.468
Ally smiled.

15
00:01:00.972 --> 00:01:04.175
"Kate did a great job spreading the word around town.

16
00:01:04.675 --> 00:01:08.778
I'm so happy this many people showed up to save the soccer field."

17
00:01:08.798 --> 00:01:14.383
"Uh, I'm not sure that's why everyone is here," Mateo said.

18
00:01:15.304 --> 00:01:17.345
Ally followed his gaze across the field.

19
00:01:17.846 --> 00:01:19.787
Those people were wearing T-shirts too.

20
00:01:20.548 --> 00:01:23.150
But theirs read People for More Parking.

21
00:01:24.711 --> 00:01:25.372
Ally frowned.

22
00:01:25.392 --> 00:01:30.036
"Why would anyone want a parking lot more than a soccer field?"

23
00:01:30.856 --> 00:01:32.097
Then her face lit up.

24
00:01:33.178 --> 00:01:34.479
"I'm going to talk to them!

25
00:01:34.919 --> 00:01:40.462
I'll use my Astralian powers to convince them that Sandville needs to keep this soccer field."

26
00:01:41.883 --> 00:01:45.526
Ally hurried over to a man who was collecting signatures for the parking lot.

27
00:01:46.526 --> 00:01:48.788
She asked why he wanted a new parking lot.

28
00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:54.692
"Since more tourists started coming to town, it's become impossible to find a parking spot."

29
00:01:55.252 --> 00:01:56.113
The man scowled.

30
00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:58.514
"Customers can't come to our stores.

31
00:01:59.155 --> 00:02:00.576
We can't park to run errands.

32
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:01.840
It's a nightmare!"

33
00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:06.101
"I didn't think of all that," Ally said.

34
00:02:06.121 --> 00:02:10.163
"But having a place for people to play soccer is important too."

35
00:02:10.183 --> 00:02:13.944
"You can't have everything, kid," the man said.

36
00:02:13.964 --> 00:02:17.065
"We'll just have to see which side collects more signatures.

37
00:02:17.785 --> 00:02:19.605
But I doubt it will be your side.

38
00:02:20.666 --> 00:02:25.607
We already have more than two hundred signatures from Sandville residents."

39
00:02:26.027 --> 00:02:26.767
Ally gasped.

40
00:02:27.227 --> 00:02:28.928
More than two hundred signatures?

41
00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:34.461
"I guess we lost," she thought as she headed back to her friends.

42
00:02:34.481 --> 00:02:39.363
"I thought I'd be able to go home and tell my parents about all the great things I

43
00:02:39.403 --> 00:02:40.423
did in Sandville.

44
00:02:40.923 --> 00:02:45.004
But now I'll have to go home and admit I messed things up."

45
00:02:47.085 --> 00:02:51.006
"Ally, what did that man say?"

46
00:02:51.306 --> 00:02:51.946
Barry asked.

47
00:02:52.786 --> 00:02:53.607
Ally shook her head.

48
00:02:53.627 --> 00:02:58.048
"That we'll have to see which side can collect more signatures.

49
00:02:58.976 --> 00:03:01.157
And they already have over two hundred!"

50
00:03:02.558 --> 00:03:03.418
Julius shrugged.

51
00:03:04.119 --> 00:03:05.660
"Then I guess we'd better get to work."

52
00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:09.802
"You think we can get more signatures than they got?"

53
00:03:10.202 --> 00:03:10.762
Ally asked.

54
00:03:10.782 --> 00:03:14.524
"We'll never know if we don't try," Julius said.

55
00:03:14.544 --> 00:03:17.786
"Julius is right," Mateo said.

56
00:03:17.806 --> 00:03:22.149
"Let's fan out around town and get as many signatures as we can."

57
00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:28.232
The soccer kids broke up into small groups and headed into town.

58
00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:33.242
Soon the only people left at the field were Ally, Barry, and Julius.

59
00:03:34.302 --> 00:03:36.023
Julius' cheeks turned pink.

60
00:03:36.763 --> 00:03:40.605
"Do you want to go to the UFO Museum with me to collect signatures, Ally?"

61
00:03:41.786 --> 00:03:45.527
Ally wasn't trying to read his mind, but she could sense something strong.

62
00:03:46.608 --> 00:03:48.288
"He likes me," she thought.

63
00:03:48.308 --> 00:03:53.751
"It's the same feeling that Mateo had for Bethany before they'd started dating."

64
00:03:55.011 --> 00:03:56.032
And she liked him back.

65
00:03:58.948 --> 00:04:02.330
"But I'm leaving soon and never coming back," Ally thought.

66
00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:06.032
"I can't explain that, and I don't want to fib again."

67
00:04:06.052 --> 00:04:09.874
"Um," Ally fumbled for words.

68
00:04:09.894 --> 00:04:12.476
"I, um, no thanks.

69
00:04:13.356 --> 00:04:15.838
Barry's going to the diner to collect signatures.

70
00:04:16.238 --> 00:04:17.699
I think I'll just go there too."

71
00:04:18.759 --> 00:04:19.860
Julius looked hurt.

72
00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:24.002
"See you later," he mumbled as he walked away.

73
00:04:24.022 --> 00:04:27.164
"Ugh!" Ally thought in frustration.

74
00:04:27.776 --> 00:04:31.998
"I hurt his feelings again maybe this time I should have told a fib!"

75
00:04:32.018 --> 00:04:35.559
"Are you ready to go collect signatures, Ally?"

76
00:04:35.859 --> 00:04:36.480
Barry asked.

77
00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:40.601
"Sure." Ally sighed.

78
00:04:42.222 --> 00:04:48.404
While Ally and Barry collected signatures outside the diner, they talked about the menu for Ally's surprise Holly

79
00:04:48.424 --> 00:04:49.065
Days party.

80
00:04:49.085 --> 00:04:53.286
"This is going to be an unusual party," Barry said.

81
00:04:53.306 --> 00:04:54.987
"That's for sure!"

82
00:04:56.468 --> 00:04:57.108
Ally laughed.

83
00:04:57.868 --> 00:04:59.269
"Barry! Can you come here, please?"

84
00:04:59.709 --> 00:05:01.410
Ray called Barry into the diner.

85
00:05:03.351 --> 00:05:05.332
A few minutes later, Barry was back.

86
00:05:07.093 --> 00:05:08.114
"What was that about?"

87
00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:09.034
Ally asked.

88
00:05:09.054 --> 00:05:11.796
"It was about me saving your party."

89
00:05:11.816 --> 00:05:14.477
"Huh? What do you mean?"

90
00:05:15.218 --> 00:05:16.519
Barry grinned proudly.

91
00:05:17.639 --> 00:05:19.740
"Ray heard us talking about a surprise party.

92
00:05:20.241 --> 00:05:24.163
He asked me who was throwing one, so I told him someone called to book a party here.

93
00:05:24.943 --> 00:05:25.924
Good idea, right?"

94
00:05:27.688 --> 00:05:30.050
"What?" Ally slapped her forehead.

95
00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:31.531
"No, Barry!

96
00:05:31.951 --> 00:05:33.812
That was a terrible idea!

97
00:05:33.832 --> 00:05:38.515
Now Ray thinks he has to cook and shop for a party that's not real!"
